msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:93
msgid ""
"Displays post metadata such as author, published/modified dates, time, "
"comments, and terms with icons, separators, and optional links."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:98
msgid "Site Title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:99
msgid ""
"Displays the site title with an optional home link, semantic heading tag, "
"responsive alignment, typography, color, and text shadow controls."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:104
msgid "Site Tagline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:105
msgid ""
"Displays the site tagline (description) with a semantic HTML tag, "
"responsive alignment, typography, color, and text shadow controls."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:110
msgid "Site Logo"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:111
msgid ""
"Displays the site logo with upload/replace support, optional home link, "
"responsive width, border, and shadow controls."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:116
msgid "Query Title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:117
msgid ""
"Displays the archive, search, or post type title for the current query, "
"with prefix and search-term options."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:122
msgid "Archive Description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:123
msgid ""
"Displays the description for the current archive such as category, tag, "
"taxonomy, or author."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:128
msgid "Query Total"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:129
msgid ""
"Displays the total number of results for the current main query, as a count "
"or range."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:134
msgid "Paragraph"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:135
msgid ""
"A standard paragraph block with advanced typography, colors, text shadow, "
"and dynamic data binding. Use for general text content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:140
msgid "Image"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:141
msgid ""
"Displays an image with full visual control including custom dimensions, "
"object-fit, opacity, CSS filters, border, shadow, and hover transition "
"effects. Also supports captions. Use when more styling control than the "
"core image block is needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:146
msgid "Button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:147
msgid ""
"A call-to-action button with a label, URL, optional icon (before or after "
"text), and full hover styling for color, background, border, and shadow. "
"Use for CTAs, download links, or any interactive link that needs custom "
"visual design."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:152
msgid "Video"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:153
msgid ""
"Embeds a video from YouTube, Vimeo, or a self-hosted file. Supports "
"autoplay, loop, lazy load, start/end time, aspect ratio, privacy mode, and "
"a custom poster image with overlay play button. Use for product demos, "
"testimonials, or media-rich sections."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:158
msgid "Google Map"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:159
msgid ""
"Embeds a Google Map for a given location with configurable zoom and height. "
"Use for contact pages, store locators, or any page that needs to display a "
"physical location."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:164
msgid "Icon List"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:165
msgid ""
"A list of icon and text pairs displayed in a column or row layout. Use for "
"feature lists, checklists, service highlights, or any bulleted content that "
"benefits from custom icons instead of plain bullets. Contains "
"icon-list-item child blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:170
msgid "Icon List Item"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:171
msgid ""
"A single icon and text row inside an Icon List block. Each item has its own "
"text, icon, and optional link. Must be placed inside an Icon List block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:177
msgid "Rating"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:178
msgid ""
"Displays a visual star (or custom icon) rating with a configurable scale "
"and decimal value. Use for product reviews, service ratings, or testimonial "
"sections."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:183
msgid "Counter"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:184
msgid ""
"An animated number that counts up to a target value on scroll. Supports a "
"prefix, suffix, thousand separator, and a title label positioned above or "
"below the number. Use for statistics sections ? e.g. \"500+ clients\", \"99 "
"percent uptime\", \"$2M raised\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:189
msgid "Countdown"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:190
msgid ""
"A live countdown to a target date/time with multiple design layouts (boxes, "
"inline, stacked, circular rings, flip clock). Toggle "
"days/hours/minutes/seconds, custom labels, and an expired message. Use for "
"launches, sales, events, and limited-time offers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:195
msgid "Progress Bar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:196
msgid ""
"An animated horizontal bar that fills to a given percentage on scroll. "
"Supports a title, an inner text label inside the fill, and custom colors. "
"Use for skills sections, fundraising progress, or any percentage-based "
"visual indicator."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:201
msgid "Social Icons"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:202
msgid ""
"A grid of social media icon links with shape options (circle, square, "
"rounded), official brand colors or custom colors, hover animations, and "
"flexible column layout. Use in headers, footers, author bios, or contact "
"sections. Contains social-icon-item child blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:207
msgid "Social Icon Item"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:208
msgid ""
"A single social network link inside a Social Icons block. Defines the "
"network (facebook, instagram, linkedin, youtube, etc.), its icon, brand "
"color, and URL. Must be placed inside a Social Icons block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:214
msgid "Accordion"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:215
msgid ""
"A collapsible accordion that can allow one or multiple items open at once. "
"Supports FAQ structured data markup for SEO. Use for FAQs, product specs, "
"or any expandable Q&A content. Contains accordion-item child blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:220
msgid "Filter Container"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:221
msgid ""
"Lets visitors search and filter the blocks inside it. Give any inner block "
"comma-separated filter terms (filterTerms attribute); the container shows a "
"search box and one button per term. Use for portfolios, FAQs, team members "
"or resource lists on a single page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:226
msgid "Accordion Item"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:227
msgid ""
"A single collapsible panel inside an Accordion block. Has a title, a "
"default-open option, and customizable expand/collapse icons. The content "
"area accepts any inner blocks. Must be placed inside an Accordion block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:233
msgid "Tab"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:234
msgid ""
"A tabbed content container with horizontal or vertical tab navigation, "
"configurable active tab, and optional icons on each tab. Use for product "
"details, service categories, pricing tiers, or any multi-section content "
"that benefits from tab navigation. Contains tab-item child blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:239
msgid "Tab Item"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:240
msgid ""
"A single tab panel inside a Tab block. Has a title, an optional icon, and a "
"default-active option. The content area accepts any inner blocks. Must be "
"placed inside a Tab block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:246
msgid "Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:247
msgid ""
"A top-level responsive navigation wrapper that automatically switches "
"between a desktop navigation menu and a mobile-friendly slide-in offcanvas "
"drawer based on a breakpoint. Acts as the primary container for site "
"headers. Contains navmenu and offcanvas child blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:252
msgid "Nav Menu"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:253
msgid ""
"Desktop navigation menu inside Navigation. Horizontal/vertical layout, item "
"styling, submenuTrigger (hover|click), and submenuRevealAnimation "
"(fade|slide|scale|soft). Children are navmenu-item blocks that may nest "
"submenu or megamenu dropdowns."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:259
msgid "Nav Menu Item"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:260
msgid ""
"Single nav link (label, url, optional icon). Parent: navmenu, offcanvas, or "
"nested submenu. May contain exactly one child: navmenu-submenu (link list) "
"or navmenu-megamenu (CPT embed) ? not both."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:266
msgid "Nav Menu Submenu"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:267
msgid ""
"Dropdown/flyout under a navmenu-item. Nested navmenu-item children only. "
"Controls: alignment, itemGap, positionAlign, offsetY/offsetX. Inside "
"offcanvas sync, renders as accordion (desktop card chrome stripped)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:273
msgid "Nav Menu Mega Menu"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:274
msgid ""
"Wide mega dropdown under a navmenu-item. Embeds a published "
"blockish_megamenu CPT via megamenuId (create CPT with manage-post). Width "
"modes: navigation|full|custom; customWidth, positionAlign, alignRelativeTo, "
"offsetY/offsetX. Mutually exclusive with navmenu-submenu on the same item."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:280
msgid "Off Canvas"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:281
msgid ""
"Mobile slide-in drawer + hamburger inside Navigation. syncWithMenu mirrors "
"sibling navmenu (including submenu/megamenu trees) as accordion. Side, "
"animation, header branding, hamburger icon. Do not put transform on the "
"root."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:287
msgid "Before/After Slider"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:288
msgid ""
"An interactive slider that lets users compare two images (a \"before\" and "
"\"after\" image) by dragging a handle horizontally."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:293
msgid "Carousel"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:294
msgid ""
"InnerBlocks carousel for hero, testimonials, or logo strips. Add Carousel "
"Slide children and build each slide with Container, Heading, Button, Image, "
"and other allowed blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:299
msgid "Carousel Slide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:300
msgid ""
"A single carousel slide with its own background/layout. Only limited "
"content blocks are allowed (no Container)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:307
msgid "Embed a reusable Blockish form (fields live on the form CPT)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:314
msgid "Text Field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:315
msgid "Single-line text input for Blockish forms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:323
msgid "Email Field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:324
msgid "Email input with validation for Blockish forms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:332
msgid "Number Field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:333
msgid "Numeric input for Blockish forms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:341
msgid "Textarea"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:342
msgid ""
"Multi-line text input field for the form block. Ideal for messages and "
"comments."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:350
msgid "Consent Checkbox"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:351
msgid "GDPR / privacy consent checkbox with optional policy link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:359
msgid "Submit Button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:360
msgid "The submit action button for the form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:368
msgid "Query Builder"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:369
msgid "Query posts and provide the results to inner Loop and Pagination blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:377
msgid "Loop"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:378
msgid "Repeats its inner template for every post in the parent Query Builder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:387
msgid "Pagination"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Config/BlocksList.php:388
msgid "Renders pagination links for the parent Query Builder query."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/WriteBlog/Config.php:14
msgid "Write Blog Post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/WriteBlog/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Writes or edits a blog post (omit post_id to create, provide it to edit; "
"defaults to post type \"post\") using WordPress CORE blocks only ? never "
"blockish custom blocks. Pass the layout as block_schema, not raw HTML "
"comments. When a schema is staged, share edit_url (not post_url) so the "
"user can review it in the canvas and accept it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/SiteInfo/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Site Info"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/SiteInfo/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Returns WordPress site name, description, URL, version, active theme, and "
"plugins."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/PostTypes/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Post Types"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/PostTypes/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Returns all registered WordPress post types with their label, public "
"visibility, and hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/RestoreRevision/Config.php:14
msgid "Restore Post Revision"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/RestoreRevision/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Restores a WordPress revision onto its parent post. Requires confirm:true. "
"Only call when the user explicitly asks to undo/restore."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageThemeJson/Config.php:14
msgid "Manage Global Styles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageThemeJson/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Apply, list, or restore the site's user global styles (wp_global_styles). "
"Pass theme_json to update. list_revisions / restore_revision_id only touch "
"that styles post ? not pages or templates. Updates are live (no "
"Accept/Discard). Install fonts with blockish/manage-fonts before setting "
"typography here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageTerm/Config.php:14
msgid "Create, Edit or Delete Term"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageTerm/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Creates a term (omit term_id), edits one (provide term_id), or deletes one "
"(provide term_id and set delete to true) within any registered taxonomy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageTemplate/Config.php:14
msgid "Create or Edit Template"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageTemplate/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Creates, updates or deletes a template or template part. Block themes: FSE "
"wp_template / wp_template_part. Classic themes with Theme Builder: same "
"type values map to TB templates and parts. Pass Blockish layouts as "
"block_schema, never raw HTML. Staged as blockish/ai-preview. After staging "
"AGENT opens edit_url once (resolves whole pending queue), waitUntil "
"domcontentloaded, wait 10?15s, then give a normal WordPress frontend view "
"URL for that template (home, a page, etc.). Settings Accept/Discard only if "
"asked. Call get-designer-workflow and get-block-docs first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManagePost/Config.php:14
msgid "Create, Edit or Delete Post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManagePost/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Creates, edits, or deletes a post. To CREATE: omit post_id but provide "
"post_title and post_type. To EDIT: provide post_id. To DELETE: provide "
"post_id and set delete to true. For Blockish layouts, pass block_schema ? "
"stages blockish/ai-preview in post_content. After staging: AGENT opens "
"edit_url once (prefer this page; resolves whole pending queue), waitUntil "
"domcontentloaded, wait 10?15s, then give post_url. Do not push "
"Accept/Discard unless asked. Never put core/template-part header/footer on "
"pages. CRITICAL: call blockish/get-designer-workflow and "
"blockish/get-block-docs before designing. For blog prose use "
"blockish/write-blog, not this tool."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManagePluginsThemes/Config.php:14
msgid "Manage Plugins & Themes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManagePluginsThemes/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Install, activate, deactivate, switch, or update WordPress.org plugins and "
"themes. Never use WP-CLI, zip URLs, GitHub, or the filesystem. Never "
"uninstall or delete. Ask the user in chat first, then pass confirm:true. "
"Slug must be the exact wordpress.org directory slug. Promoted: ACF "
"`advanced-custom-fields` (install+activate), WooCommerce `woocommerce` "
"(install+activate), Blockish Forms `blockish-forms` (Pro ? activate only if "
"already installed), Blockish Dynamicity `blockish-dynamicity` (Pro ? "
"activate only). After install or activate of those four, you MUST tell the "
"user to fully restart the AI software they are using (Cursor, Claude "
"Desktop, ChatGPT, etc.) or reconnect Blockish MCP ? new abilities will not "
"appear in this session. Cannot deactivate Blockish core (`blockish`). "
"Cannot deactivate themes (switch instead). Update only when the user "
"explicitly asked to update."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManagePattern/Config.php:16
msgid "Create or Update a Component Pattern"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManagePattern/Config.php:17
msgid ""
"Use this tool to create or update reusable component patterns (Hero, "
"Footer, etc.). Stages block_schema onto the wp_block as a "
"blockish/ai-preview (previousSchema + pendingSchema). New page build: stage "
"patterns, then stage the page with refs, then open the PAGE edit_url once "
"(any editor resolves the whole pending queue ? do not open every pattern "
"editor). If the user is already editing a parent page/template that refs "
"this pattern, also re-stage that parent with its current schema after "
"updating the pattern."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageOptions/Config.php:14
msgid "Manage WordPress & Blockish Options"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageOptions/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Retrieve or update allowlisted WordPress core settings and Blockish "
"options. Cannot change siteurl or home (those break the site). Omit action "
"(or pass \"get\") to read; pass action \"update\" with values to write."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageMedia/Config.php:13
msgid "Create, Edit or Delete Media"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageMedia/Config.php:14
msgid ""
"Creates, edits, or deletes a media attachment (images and common videos). "
"Preferred create path for a file on the AI/client machine: upload it to a "
"third-party temporary file host, then pass the direct public HTTPS URL in "
"url. Do not use client disk paths or base64 for remote MCP. file_path is "
"WordPress-server only. To EDIT: provide attachment_id and title/alt_text "
"(alt_text for images). To DELETE: provide attachment_id and set delete to "
"true. Allowed: jpg/jpeg/png/gif/webp + mp4/webm/mov."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageInteractions/Config.php:14
msgid "Manage Interactions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageInteractions/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Get or update Blockish interaction libraries: site-wide (global) or for a "
"specific page/post (page). Block-level rules still use the interactionData "
"attribute on blocks via manage-post / manage-pattern."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageFonts/Config.php:14
msgid "Manage Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageFonts/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Installs, updates, activates, deactivates, or deletes custom fonts in the "
"WordPress Font Library and Global Styles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageComments/Config.php:14
msgid "Manage Comments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageComments/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Retrieve, create, update, or delete WordPress comments (approve, spam, "
"trash)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageClass/Config.php:14
msgid "Create, Update or Delete CSS Class"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ManageClass/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Upserts reusable Class Manager classes from raw CSS. Just send css ? the "
"class name is read from each selector (e.g. \".hero-title { ? }\" ? class "
"\"hero-title\"), and the class is created if new or updated (full replace) "
"if it already exists. One stylesheet may declare several classes; each "
"\".name\" root becomes its own class, while :hover / descendants (\".name "
"h2\") become that class's children. You never pass action/name/post_id for "
"normal styling, and never write style objects or child posts. Returns the "
"affected classes (post_id, name, css_selector, combined css) under "
"\"classes\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/JsonHelper/Config.php:14
msgid "JSON Helper"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/JsonHelper/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Helper to safely stringify a JSON object/array into a string, or parse a "
"stringified JSON back into an object. Use this to avoid manual string "
"escaping errors when building schemas for typography, backgrounds, etc."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/JsonHelper/Callbacks.php:23
msgid "Failed to stringify JSON data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/JsonHelper/Callbacks.php:29
msgid "Data must be a string for parse action."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/JsonHelper/Callbacks.php:33
msgid "Failed to parse JSON string: "
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/JsonHelper/Callbacks.php:38
msgid "Action must be stringify or parse."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetThemeJsonDocs/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Theme JSON Docs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetThemeJsonDocs/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Fetches the active theme's merged theme.json data (palette, typography, "
"spacing, layouts). Use this before managing global styles to understand the "
"active theme's variables and schema."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetTemplates/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Templates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetTemplates/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Fetches templates and template parts for the active theme. Block themes: "
"Site Editor (wp_template / wp_template_part). Classic themes with Theme "
"Builder enabled: blockish_tb templates and parts. Same tool either way ? "
"check `backend` in the response (`fse` or `theme_builder`)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetTaxonomies/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Taxonomies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetTaxonomies/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Returns all registered WordPress taxonomies with their label, public "
"visibility, and hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetRevisions/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Post Revisions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetRevisions/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Lists recent WordPress revisions for a post/page so you can restore a "
"previous live version after a bad content change. Only use when the user "
"asks to undo or inspect history."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetPosts/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Posts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetPosts/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Reads existing posts, pages or any registered post type, filterable by "
"post_type, search, status and pagination, or fetch one by post_id. To get "
"full content + schema you MUST pass post_id (not id, include, or WP REST "
"list params)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetMedia/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Media"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetMedia/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Lists existing items in the WordPress Media Library, filterable by search, "
"mime_type and pagination."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetMagicLogin/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Magic Login URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetIcons/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Icons"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetIcons/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Searches the built-in Font Awesome icon library and returns the SVG paths "
"so you can use them with the Icon type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetFonts/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetFonts/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Fetches all installed fonts (Font Families and Font Faces) along with "
"theme-provided fonts from global styles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetDesignerWorkflow/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Designer Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetDesignerWorkflow/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Call this tool before starting any website design task to get the strict "
"workflow and best practices (SOP)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetClasses/Config.php:14
msgid "Get CSS Classes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetClasses/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Returns parent Class Manager classes (keyed by post_id) with name, "
"css_selector, and combined raw css ? including :hover / descendants "
"rewritten as .name:hover etc. Child posts are internal; AI only sees this "
"CSS surface. Call before creating to avoid duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetClassUsage/Config.php:12
msgid "Get Class Manager Usage"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetClassUsage/Config.php:13
msgid ""
"Reports where each Class Manager parent class is attached (posts, pages, "
"patterns, templates, forms). Filter by post_id or name. Also returns an "
"unused list for cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetClassManagerDocs/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Class Manager Docs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetClassManagerDocs/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Returns the Class Manager reference ? raw CSS create/update via "
"manage-class (!important ? customCss), attaching classes by name, usage "
"tracking (get-class-usage), unused sweep, and template-library class "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetAiPreviewPending/Config.php:12
msgid "Get AI Preview Pending Count"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetAiPreviewPending/Config.php:13
msgid ""
"Reports how many AI Preview designs are not finalized yet. Once resolved "
"(an editor was opened), a staged design is already live on the frontend for "
"every visitor; Accept only finalizes it (drops the saved previous version "
"Discard would restore). Accept is never required to continue. This tool "
"never Accepts or Discards."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/FetchGoogleFonts/Config.php:14
msgid "Fetch Google Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/FetchGoogleFonts/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Fetches exact font face data from the official WordPress Google Fonts "
"collection. Use this to prepare valid payloads for manage-fonts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ExtensionsInfo/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Extensions Info"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ExtensionsInfo/Config.php:15
msgid "Returns total, active and inactive Blockish extension counts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/FetchCloudTemplates/Config.php:14
msgid "Fetch Cloud Templates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/FetchCloudTemplates/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Fetches boilerplate design templates (patterns and pages) from the Blockish "
"Cloud Template Library. Designs may include dependencies.patterns, "
"dependencies.forms, and dependencies.classes (cloud id + content/css). "
"Recreate those as local wp_block / blockish_form / blockish-classes posts, "
"remap ref/formId/classManager ids cloud?local, then adapt the schema to the "
"user request. CRITICAL: Never use cloud IDs as-is on the destination site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetAutomationGuideline/Config.php:16
msgid "Get Automation Guideline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/GetAutomationGuideline/Config.php:17
msgid ""
"Provides browser automation + verify-loop instructions for resolving staged "
"AI previews (editor open, wait 10?15s, frontend screenshot). MUST BE READ "
"before browser automation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/BlockDocs/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Block Docs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/BlockDocs/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Returns Blockish core docs plus attribute docs for the blocks you name. "
"block_names is REQUIRED ? never call without it (full library dump is "
"disabled to save context). If omitted or empty, returns an error plus the "
"blocks/extensions catalogs so you can choose names and retry."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/BlocksInfo/Config.php:14
msgid "Get Blocks Info"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/BlocksInfo/Config.php:15
msgid ""
"Returns all Blockish blocks keyed by name, each with its status and an "
"optional \"parent\" key marking child/inner blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ConvertCss/Config.php:12
msgid "Convert CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Abilities/ConvertCss/Config.php:13
msgid ""
"Convert CSS ? Blockish style attributes. Prefer action css_to_schema: build "
"a full block_schema with content attrs + per-node css using {{ROOT}}, "
"convert once, push the returned schema to manage-pattern / manage-post. "
"Also supports single-block css_to_attributes / attributes_to_css. Style "
"only ? markup and content attrs come from get-block-docs."
msgstr ""

